.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
data/
reports/*.json
runtime/

# .env backups. Three of these were committed (195f9d6, 4b5b965) because the
# ignore rule matched only the exact name `.env` - a timestamped copy made
# before editing it sailed straight past and carried the live credentials
# into a public repository.
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak
*.env.backup
.env.eth
# PER-INSTANCE CREDENTIAL FILES, by pattern rather than by name. `.env.eth` was
# listed individually, so `.env.gold`, `.env.silver` and `.env.sol` - three new
# instances added 2026-09-25 - were not covered. That is the SAME shape of gap
# that leaked the credentials in the first place: an ignore rule matching only
# the exact names that existed when it was written. The negation keeps the
# committed template visible.
.env.*
!.env.example
runtime-*/
eth15.db*
